# Plan completion review gate

When executing a plan from `docs/implementation/plans/`:

1. Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and `.cursor/skills/multi-model-plan-review/SKILL.md`
2. Work on a **feature branch** in the main repo (not a worktree): `git checkout -b feat/<name>` from `main`
3. Phase A: thermo-nuclear self review → write `*-review-self-thermonuclear.md` with `## Verdict: APPROVED`
4. Verify: `./scripts/plan-review-check-phase-a.sh . docs/implementation/plans/<plan>.md`
5. **Return to the user** for feedback — do **not** run `plan-review.sh` (Phase B) autonomously
6. After user feedback: fix **every suggestion (all severities, including low priority)** → quality gate → re-run Phase A if code changed → merge when user directs
7. **Phase C:** delete interim review artifacts → merge into `main` → delete feature branch

## Fix-everything policy (Phase A and user feedback)

Implement **all** findings and **all** feedback items — every priority, severity, and label (P0–P2+, Critical/Major/Minor, maintenance smell, low priority, nice-to-have, deferred, 🟡/🟢). **Do not defer** because something looks optional.

**Only exception:** you **explicitly disagree** with a specific item and document why (Phase A verdict: **Explicit disagreements** section). Undocumented skips are forbidden.

**Forbidden:** APPROVED verdicts with “Deferred” / “non-blocking” lists without documented disagreement per item; merging while any non-disagreed feedback remains open.

See `.cursor/skills/multi-model-plan-review/SKILL.md` for full rules.

**Forbidden:** using a worktree for plan implementation by default; running `plan-review.sh` as part of the orchestrator gate; committing interim review artifacts to `main`.
